{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SeraeLhxxihU6sD9TB7bV8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Brief: time tracking widget\n2\t\n3\ttype: feature\n4\tid: willing\n5\tbranch: feature/willing_time-tracking-widget\n6\tdate: 2026-10-29\n7\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\n8\t\n9\t## What\n10\t\n11\tA second home-screen widget: **time tracking**. It shows the running timer\n12\t(project, live elapsed time, a stop button) and the user's projects, each\n13\twith a start button. Starting a project while another timer runs switches to\n14\tit in one tap. Tapping a row (outside its button) opens that project in the\n15\tapp.\n16\t\n17\tDepends on [[android-widget-foundation-multiple-kinds]] (native support for\n18\tseveral widget kinds) and on the API and app jobs below, which live in other\n19\trepos. Their full contract is in this entry.\n20\t\n21\t**Prerequisite, done by a human before this job starts:** `frontend/` is\n22\tvendored from `solyto/app` with the job \"time tracking widget: refresh on\n23\tchanges, route keys\". Confirm that `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts`\n24\thandles `time_tracking_project`; do not run `scripts/vendor.sh` (`../app` is\n25\tnot available here). If it is missing, stop and ask.\n26\t\n27\t## Why\n28\t\n29\tA user asked to start and stop time tracking from the home screen.\n30\t\n31\t## Contract with the API and the app\n32\t\n33\tThe API and the app are not visible from here. Build against this exactly.\n34\t\n35\t### `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/time-tracking`\n36\t\n37\tSame headers, envelope and status codes as Your Day\n38\t(`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`, `Accept: application/json`,\n39\t`X-Client-Version`; 200 / 401 / 404 / 426 / 429 / 5xx as in\n40\t`android-widget-foundation-your-day.md`). `data`:\n41\t\n42\t```\n43\t{\n44\t  \"kind\": \"time-tracking\", \"schema_version\": 1, \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n45\t  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },      // translated\n46\t  \"sections\": [\n47\t    { \"key\": \"running\", \"title\": \"…\", \"rows\": [{  // only while a timer runs; one row\n48\t        \"id\": \"<entry uuid>\",\n49\t        \"title\": \"<project title>\",\n50\t        \"subtitle\": \"<entry description>\",       // optional\n51\t        \"at\": \"<started_at, ISO 8601 with offset>\",\n52\t        \"live\": \"elapsed\",\n53\t        \"all_day\": false,\n54\t        \"color\": \"#RRGGBB\",                       // optional\n55\t        \"icon\": \"timer\",\n56\t        \"route\": { \"key\": \"time_tracking_project\", \"id\": \"<project uuid>\" },\n57\t        \"action\": { \"type\": \"button\", \"key\": \"time_tracking.stop\", \"icon\": \"stop\" }\n58\t    }] },\n59\t    { \"key\": \"projects\", \"title\": \"…\", \"rows\": [{  // up to 20, most recently used first\n60\t        \"id\": \"<project uuid>\",\n61\t        \"title\": \"<project title>\",\n62\t        \"all_day\": false,\n63\t        \"color\": \"#RRGGBB\",                       // optional\n64\t        \"route\": { \"key\": \"time_tracking_project\", \"id\": \"<project uuid>\" },\n65\t        \"action\": { \"type\": \"button\", \"key\": \"time_tracking.start\", \"icon\": \"play\" }\n66\t    }] }\n67\t  ]\n68\t}\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\t- **No `refresh_at`** for this widget: it is optional in the format.\n72\t- The running project is not repeated in `projects`.\n73\t- `sections: []` means no projects and no timer: show `labels.empty`.\n74\t- New in the format, all backwards compatible (`schema_version` stays 1):\n75\t  `live: \"elapsed\"`, `color`, action type `button` with `icon` (`play` |\n76\t  `stop`), row icon `timer`. Unknown values stay ignored, as before.\n77\t\n78\t### Actions\n79\t\n80\t`POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{row id}`, no body, same headers:\n81\t\n82\t- `time_tracking.start/<project uuid>`: starts that project. If another timer\n83\t  runs, the server stops it first. Already running: success, no change.\n84\t- `time_tracking.stop/<entry uuid>`: stops the timer. Already stopped:\n85\t  success, no change.\n86\t\n87\tStatus codes as for `todo.complete`: 200 done (also for no-ops) → re-fetch\n88\tall placed widgets; 401 → signed out; 403/404 → re-fetch; 426 → \"update the\n89\tapp\"; 429/5xx/offline → revert, short error state.\n90\t\n91\t### Route keys (handled by the app's widget bridge)\n92\t\n93\tPass `route` through unchanged with `navigate`: `time_tracking_project` + a\n94\tproject UUID opens that project; `time_tracking` (no id) opens the time\n95\ttracking page.\n96\t\n97\t## Steps\n98\t\n99\t1. **Kind:** register `time-tracking` (path `/api/v1/widgets/time-tracking`)\n100\t   in the kind registry from [[android-widget-foundation-multiple-kinds]].\n101\t2. **Parser:** read the new fields (`live`, `color`, `button` actions with\n102\t   `icon`, icon `timer`) in the generic payload parser. Your Day ignores them.\n103\t3. **Widget** (`TimeTrackingWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`, list via\n104\t   `RemoteCollectionItems` like Your Day):\n105\t   - header with `labels.title` and \"updated at\", tapping it opens the app;\n106\t   - section titles; rows with title, optional subtitle, a color dot (from\n107\t     `color`, else the accent color), and the action button on the right\n108\t     (`play` / `stop` icons, our own vector drawables, not platform widgets);\n109\t   - the running row shows the elapsed time with a `Chronometer`\n110\t     (`setChronometer`, base computed from `at`), so it counts up without\n111\t     fetching; it is visibly highlighted;\n112\t   - `labels.empty` when there are no sections;\n113\t   - the same states as Your Day (loading, signed out, unsupported server,\n114\t     update the app, couldn't load, outdated);\n115\t   - light and dark; resizable; `appwidget-provider` XML with a preview and\n116\t     description; a sensible default size (for example 3×2).\n117\t4. **Buttons:** reuse the action plumbing from tap-to-complete. Tapping a\n118\t   button shows that row as busy (button disabled) at once, runs the action in\n119\t   the background, then re-fetches all placed widgets. On failure: revert and\n120\t   show the short error state. Taps on a busy row are ignored.\n121\t5. **Row taps** (outside the button) send `navigate` with the row's `route`,\n122\t   as in Your Day.\n123\t6. **Strings** in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`: picker name and\n124\t   description, the buttons' content descriptions. Content text comes from the\n125\t   server. New strings go to the translator.\n126\t7. **Manual checks:** place it next to Your Day; start a project (the timer\n127\t   counts up); start another project (switches); stop; start and stop in the\n128\t   app (the widget follows within seconds); tap a row (opens the project, warm\n129\t   and cold start); no projects (empty text); airplane mode while tapping\n130\t   start (revert + error); logout; API 24 and 34+; light and dark.\n131\t\n132\t## Out of scope\n133\t\n134\t- NFC tags and Samsung Routines (mentioned in the original request).\n135\t- Descriptions or categories from the widget.\n136\t- Changes to Your Day.\n137\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3be7bc9d-7930-4dcf-a4f0-60bdfff056b9","uuid":"d946a1c2-0185-41f4-a3a0-bcbfa3af7e26","timestamp":"2026-10-29T20:13:20.363Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/willing_time-tracking-widget/brief.md","content":"# Brief: time tracking widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: willing\nbranch: feature/willing_time-tracking-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nA second home-screen widget: **time tracking**. It shows the running timer\n(project, live elapsed time, a stop button) and the user's projects, each\nwith a start button. Starting a project while another timer runs switches to\nit in one tap. Tapping a row (outside its button) opens that project in the\napp.\n\nDepends on [[android-widget-foundation-multiple-kinds]] (native support for\nseveral widget kinds) and on the API and app jobs below, which live in other\nrepos. Their full contract is in this entry.\n\n**Prerequisite, done by a human before this job starts:** `frontend/` is\nvendored from `solyto/app` with the job \"time tracking widget: refresh on\nchanges, route keys\". Confirm that `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts`\nhandles `time_tracking_project`; do not run `scripts/vendor.sh` (`../app` is\nnot available here). If it is missing, stop and ask.\n\n## Why\n\nA user asked to start and stop time tracking from the home screen.\n\n## Contract with the API and the app\n\nThe API and the app are not visible from here. Build against this exactly.\n\n### `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/time-tracking`\n\nSame headers, envelope and status codes as Your Day\n(`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`, `Accept: application/json`,\n`X-Client-Version`; 200 / 401 / 404 / 426 / 429 / 5xx as in\n`android-widget-foundation-your-day.md`). `data`:\n\n```\n{\n  \"kind\": \"time-tracking\", \"schema_version\": 1, \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },      // translated\n  \"sections\": [\n    { \"key\": \"running\", \"title\": \"…\", \"rows\": [{  // only while a timer runs; one row\n        \"id\": \"<entry uuid>\",\n        \"title\": \"<project title>\",\n        \"subtitle\": \"<entry description>\",       // optional\n        \"at\": \"<started_at, ISO 8601 with offset>\",\n        \"live\": \"elapsed\",\n        \"all_day\": false,\n        \"color\": \"#RRGGBB\",                       // optional\n        \"icon\": \"timer\",\n        \"route\": { \"key\": \"time_tracking_project\", \"id\": \"<project uuid>\" },\n        \"action\": { \"type\": \"button\", \"key\": \"time_tracking.stop\", \"icon\": \"stop\" }\n    }] },\n    { \"key\": \"projects\", \"title\": \"…\", \"rows\": [{  // up to 20, most recently used first\n        \"id\": \"<project uuid>\",\n        \"title\": \"<project title>\",\n        \"all_day\": false,\n        \"color\": \"#RRGGBB\",                       // optional\n        \"route\": { \"key\": \"time_tracking_project\", \"id\": \"<project uuid>\" },\n        \"action\": { \"type\": \"button\", \"key\": \"time_tracking.start\", \"icon\": \"play\" }\n    }] }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n- **No `refresh_at`** for this widget: it is optional in the format.\n- The running project is not repeated in `projects`.\n- `sections: []` means no projects and no timer: show `labels.empty`.\n- New in the format, all backwards compatible (`schema_version` stays 1):\n  `live: \"elapsed\"`, `color`, action type `button` with `icon` (`play` |\n  `stop`), row icon `timer`. Unknown values stay ignored, as before.\n\n### Actions\n\n`POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{row id}`, no body, same headers:\n\n- `time_tracking.start/<project uuid>`: starts that project. If another timer\n  runs, the server stops it first. Already running: success, no change.\n- `time_tracking.stop/<entry uuid>`: stops the timer. Already stopped:\n  success, no change.\n\nStatus codes as for `todo.complete`: 200 done (also for no-ops) → re-fetch\nall placed widgets; 401 → signed out; 403/404 → re-fetch; 426 → \"update the\napp\"; 429/5xx/offline → revert, short error state.\n\n### Route keys (handled by the app's widget bridge)\n\nPass `route` through unchanged with `navigate`: `time_tracking_project` + a\nproject UUID opens that project; `time_tracking` (no id) opens the time\ntracking page.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Kind:** register `time-tracking` (path `/api/v1/widgets/time-tracking`)\n   in the kind registry from [[android-widget-foundation-multiple-kinds]].\n2. **Parser:** read the new fields (`live`, `color`, `button` actions with\n   `icon`, icon `timer`) in the generic payload parser. Your Day ignores them.\n3. **Widget** (`TimeTrackingWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`, list via\n   `RemoteCollectionItems` like Your Day):\n   - header with `labels.title` and \"updated at\", tapping it opens the app;\n   - section titles; rows with title, optional subtitle, a color dot (from\n     `color`, else the accent color), and the action button on the right\n     (`play` / `stop` icons, our own vector drawables, not platform widgets);\n   - the running row shows the elapsed time with a `Chronometer`\n     (`setChronometer`, base computed from `at`), so it counts up without\n     fetching; it is visibly highlighted;\n   - `labels.empty` when there are no sections;\n   - the same states as Your Day (loading, signed out, unsupported server,\n     update the app, couldn't load, outdated);\n   - light and dark; resizable; `appwidget-provider` XML with a preview and\n     description; a sensible default size (for example 3×2).\n4. **Buttons:** reuse the action plumbing from tap-to-complete. Tapping a\n   button shows that row as busy (button disabled) at once, runs the action in\n   the background, then re-fetches all placed widgets. On failure: revert and\n   show the short error state. Taps on a busy row are ignored.\n5. **Row taps** (outside the button) send `navigate` with the row's `route`,\n   as in Your Day.\n6. **Strings** in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`: picker name and\n   description, the buttons' content descriptions. Content text comes from the\n   server. New strings go to the translator.\n7. **Manual checks:** place it next to Your Day; start a project (the timer\n   counts up); start another project (switches); stop; start and stop in the\n   app (the widget follows within seconds); tap a row (opens the project, warm\n   and cold start); no projects (empty text); airplane mode while tapping\n   start (revert + error); logout; API 24 and 34+; light and dark.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- NFC tags and Samsung Routines (mentioned in the original request).\n- Descriptions or categories from the widget.\n- Changes to Your Day.\n","numLines":137,"startLine":1,"totalLines":137}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SeraeLhxxihU6sD9TB7bV8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
