{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nbrief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n# Brief: time tracking widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: willing\nbranch: feature/willing_time-tracking-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nA second home-screen widget: **time tracking**. It shows the running timer\n(project, live elapsed time, a stop button) and the user's projects, each\nwith a start button. Starting a project while another timer runs switches to\nit in one tap. Tapping a row (outside its button) opens that project in the\napp.\n\nDepends on [[android-widget-foundation-multiple-kinds]] (native support for\nseveral widget kinds) and on the API and app jobs below, which live in other\nrepos. Their full contract is in this entry.\n\n**Prerequisite, done by a human before this job starts:** `frontend/` is\nvendored from `solyto/app` with the job \"time tracking widget: refresh on\nchanges, route keys\". Confirm that `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts`\nhandles `time_tracking_project`; do not run `scripts/vendor.sh` (`../app` is\nnot available here). If it is missing, stop and ask.\n\n## Why\n\nA user asked to start and stop time tracking from the home screen.\n\n## Contract with the API and the app\n\nThe API and the app are not visible from here. Build against this exactly.\n\n### `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/time-tracking`\n\nSame headers, envelope and status codes as Your Day\n(`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`, `Accept: application/json`,\n`X-Client-Version`; 200 / 401 / 404 / 426 / 429 / 5xx as in\n`android-widget-foundation-your-day.md`). `data`:\n\n```\n{\n  \"kind\": \"time-tracking\", \"schema_version\": 1, \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },      // translated\n  \"sections\": [\n    { \"key\": \"running\", \"title\": \"…\", \"rows\": [{  // only while a timer runs; one row\n        \"id\": \"<entry uuid>\",\n        \"title\": \"<project title>\",\n        \"subtitle\": \"<entry description>\",       // optional\n        \"at\": \"<started_at, ISO 8601 with offset>\",\n        \"live\": \"elapsed\",\n        \"all_day\": false,\n        \"color\": \"#RRGGBB\",                       // optional\n        \"icon\": \"timer\",\n        \"route\": { \"key\": \"time_tracking_project\", \"id\": \"<project uuid>\" },\n        \"action\": { \"type\": \"button\", \"key\": \"time_tracking.stop\", \"icon\": \"stop\" }\n    }] },\n    { \"key\": \"projects\", \"title\": \"…\", \"rows\": [{  // up to 20, most recently used first\n        \"id\": \"<project uuid>\",\n        \"title\": \"<project title>\",\n        \"all_day\": false,\n        \"color\": \"#RRGGBB\",                       // optional\n        \"route\": { \"key\": \"time_tracking_project\", \"id\": \"<project uuid>\" },\n        \"action\": { \"type\": \"button\", \"key\": \"time_tracking.start\", \"icon\": \"play\" }\n    }] }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n- **No `refresh_at`** for this widget: it is optional in the format.\n- The running project is not repeated in `projects`.\n- `sections: []` means no projects and no timer: show `labels.empty`.\n- New in the format, all backwards compatible (`schema_version` stays 1):\n  `live: \"elapsed\"`, `color`, action type `button` with `icon` (`play` |\n  `stop`), row icon `timer`. Unknown values stay ignored, as before.\n\n### Actions\n\n`POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/{key}/{row id}`, no body, same headers:\n\n- `time_tracking.start/<project uuid>`: starts that project. If another timer\n  runs, the server stops it first. Already running: success, no change.\n- `time_tracking.stop/<entry uuid>`: stops the timer. Already stopped:\n  success, no change.\n\nStatus codes as for `todo.complete`: 200 done (also for no-ops) → re-fetch\nall placed widgets; 401 → signed out; 403/404 → re-fetch; 426 → \"update the\napp\"; 429/5xx/offline → revert, short error state.\n\n### Route keys (handled by the app's widget bridge)\n\nPass `route` through unchanged with `navigate`: `time_tracking_project` + a\nproject UUID opens that project; `time_tracking` (no id) opens the time\ntracking page.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Kind:** register `time-tracking` (path `/api/v1/widgets/time-tracking`)\n   in the kind registry from [[android-widget-foundation-multiple-kinds]].\n2. **Parser:** read the new fields (`live`, `color`, `button` actions with\n   `icon`, icon `timer`) in the generic payload parser. Your Day ignores them.\n3. **Widget** (`TimeTrackingWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`, list via\n   `RemoteCollectionItems` like Your Day):\n   - header with `labels.title` and \"updated at\", tapping it opens the app;\n   - section titles; rows with title, optional subtitle, a color dot (from\n     `color`, else the accent color), and the action button on the right\n     (`play` / `stop` icons, our own vector drawables, not platform widgets);\n   - the running row shows the elapsed time with a `Chronometer`\n     (`setChronometer`, base computed from `at`), so it counts up without\n     fetching; it is visibly highlighted;\n   - `labels.empty` when there are no sections;\n   - the same states as Your Day (loading, signed out, unsupported server,\n     update the app, couldn't load, outdated);\n   - light and dar\n\n... [9330 characters truncated] ...\n\nand needs approval. It is not planned here.\n- **\"Widget follows within seconds\":** this relies on the existing\n  `refresh` → `WidgetWork.fetchNow` path, which re-fetches every placed kind.\n  No new code is expected; it just needs verifying.\n## Summary\n\nA second home-screen widget, **time tracking**. It is registered as the\n`time-tracking` kind. It shows the running timer (highlighted row, a live\n`Chronometer`, a stop button) and the projects, each with a start button. It\nreuses the existing fetch, cache, action and route plumbing. Prerequisite\nconfirmed: `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` handles `time_tracking` and\n`time_tracking_project`. No `frontend/` edits were made, and `vendor.sh` was not\nrun.\n\n**Not built or device-tested.** This environment has no JDK and no Android SDK,\nso neither `./gradlew assembleDebug` nor lint could run. The XML files were\nchecked only for well-formedness. Someone needs to build and run the manual\nchecks from brief step 7 before merging.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `WidgetPayload.java` now reads row `live` (`elapsed`), `at` (via\n`IsoTime.parse`, -1 if invalid), `color` (strict `#RRGGBB` → opaque ARGB,\notherwise `NO_COLOR`), row icon `timer`, and action type `button` with `icon`\n`play`|`stop`. Any other icon means the row gets no action. The `Item`\nconstructor and the section-header call site were updated. `findAction` works\nfor button rows unchanged.\n\nTASK-2: In `YourDayWidgetProvider.java`, the checkbox is bound only for `check`\nactions, so a `button` row never gets a checkbox. Nothing else in Your Day\nchanged.\n\nTASK-3: `WidgetActionReceiver.java` accepts `button` actions. The\n\"already checked\" short-circuit now applies only to `check`. The existing\nvalidation (key/id format, row present in the cached payload with the same\ntype/key/id, state OK, busy rows rejected by `startAction`) is unchanged.\n`WidgetActionWorker` is unchanged: 200/403/404 → re-fetch all kinds, 401 →\nsigned out, 426 → update app, everything else → revert + error.\n\nTASK-4: `WidgetKind.java` has a new `TIME_TRACKING(\"time-tracking\", …, \"running\", \"projects\")`.\n\nTASK-5: New drawables `ic_widget_play`, `ic_widget_stop` (filled accent\ncircles, our own Lucide-based vectors), `ic_widget_timer`, `widget_color_dot`\n(white oval, tinted at runtime) and `widget_running_background`. A new color\n`widget_running` (accent at low alpha) has light and dark values.\n\nTASK-6: New `TimeTrackingWidgetProvider.java`, modeled on Your Day, with the\nsame state/message logic. New layouts `widget_time_tracking.xml`,\n`widget_time_tracking_row.xml`, `widget_time_tracking_section.xml` and\n`widget_time_tracking_preview.xml`. I gave this widget its own section layout\ninstead of reusing Your Day's. It has the same 6dp horizontal inset as the rows,\nso titles line up with the highlighted running row.\n- Every row explicitly sets its subtitle, dot tint (`color`, else\n  `widget_accent`), background (highlight only when `live == elapsed` with a\n  valid `at`), timer icon, chronometer (running or stopped + GONE), button\n  image/content description/alpha/enabled, and route fill-in. This prevents\n  stale state in recycled views.\n- Chronometer base: `elapsedRealtime() - max(0, now - at)`.\n- PendingIntent request codes are 3 and 4 (Your Day uses 1 and 2).\n\nTASK-7: New `xml/time_tracking_widget_info.xml` (description, preview layout\nplus `drawable/widget_time_tracking_preview.xml` fallback, resizable, default\n3×2: `minWidth` 180dp / `minHeight` 110dp). Receiver registered in\n`AndroidManifest.xml` with `exported=\"false\"`.\n\nTASK-8: New strings `widget_time_tracking_name`,\n`widget_time_tracking_description`, `widget_action_start`, `widget_action_stop`\nand `widget_time_tracking_failed` in `values`, `values-de`, `values-fr`,\n`values-es` and `values-it`.\n\nTASK-9: Build and manual checks were **not run** (no JDK/SDK here). None of the\nchecks from brief step 7 are verified.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **Needs a build and a device run.** Points to watch:\n  - `Chronometer` inside `RemoteCollectionItems` on API 24 and 34+.\n  - `setImageAlpha`/`setEnabled`/`setColorFilter`/`setBackgroundResource` via\n    RemoteViews.\n  - The preview layout on Android 12+.\n  - All of the brief step 7 checks.\n- **Error string:** the open question in tasks.md defaulted to reusing\n  `widget_action_failed`. I added `widget_time_tracking_failed` (\"Couldn't\n  update\") instead, because the existing German string (\"Abhaken\n  fehlgeschlagen\") means \"checking off failed\", which is wrong for start/stop.\n  