{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX9WuJBU1dv9rKVczyXp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've approved the time tracking widget code, but it has never been built or run. The environment has no JDK or Android SDK, so the review was static only.\n\n**What I found:** I read every change on the branch against the brief and found no code that needs to change. Tasks 1–8 pass. Task 9 (build and manual checks) is only partial, because neither the developer nor I could run it.\n\n**Two deviations, both justified:**\n- The widget has its own section-title layout instead of reusing Your Day's, so the titles line up with the highlighted running row. Your Day is untouched.\n- There's a new error string, \"Couldn't update\", instead of reusing \"Couldn't complete\". The German version of the old one (\"Abhaken fehlgeschlagen\") means \"checking off failed\", which reads wrong for start/stop.\n\n**Before merging, someone with an Android toolchain needs to:**\n1. Run `cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug` (plus lint) and confirm it builds.\n2. Run the manual checks from brief step 7. The main risks are the live timer and the dimmed/disabled button inside the widget list on API 24 and 34+, and the widget picker preview on Android 12+.\n\nThe new German, French, Spanish and Italian strings are the developer's own translations and still need a native-speaker check.\n\nThe verdict is in `verdict.md` and committed as `076c8b8`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":206,"cache_read_input_tokens":59781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":206},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eae841d1-6e55-4c0c-b998-d89bceca39e1","